  "status": "Foreground body-pose acceleration is enabled by default for normal imported-video jobs; no experiment flag required. Both devices restored to normal app UI.",
  "changes": [
    "ContactPoseComputePolicy follows video-job foreground state in normal builds, while explicit accuracy-comparison baselines remain CPU unless opted in.",
    "ContactObservationStore prepares a CPU request for video jobs and reuses a separate automatic Vision request while foreground; a transition failure retries the same pixels once on CPU before producing landmarks.",
    "Video jobs keep their cached poses and counter state when switching. No video lease means the existing live-camera Vision configuration and combined warmup path remain in place.",
    "Pose profiling is observational and no longer classifies normal analysis as an experiment. Normal disk cache and prediction reuse stay enabled.",
    "The pipeline cache signature includes video-pose-lifecycle-v1 so old CPU-era inference is not silently treated as a result of the new policy."
